:'''Qingque:''' This is the Matrix of Prescience &mdash; a large-scale jade abacus calculation terminal. It's the pride and joy of the Divination Commission.
:'''Welt:''' We've heard the term "jade abacus" a few times now. Would you mind explaining what it is, Miss Qingque?
:'''Qingque:''' A jade abacus is just... a jade abacus!
:'''Qingque:''' Eh-he, that's a good question, Mr. Yang &mdash; it might take me a minute to give you an answer. Let me think...
:'''Qingque:''' The book ''Glimpses Into the Beyond'' describes it as "living jade engraved with symbols for divination into the unknown."
:'''Qingque:''' Just like engraving a seal, the craftsmen of the Xianzhou Artisanship Commission carve faint symbols into pieces of jade, and then insert them into machines to get them to operate according to a certain intention.
:'''Qingque:''' Some jade abacuses are small enough to fit inside bracelets and jewelry. We put the bigger ones into instruments of calculation so we can simulate the future and learn from the past.
:'''Qingque:''' Take the Matrix of Prescience here as an example. As long as sufficient information is provided, it can answer questions on anything &mdash; from the evolution of natural phenomena to the metabolism of living things.
:'''Qingque:''' They say the theory behind the symbols was handed down by Nous, the Wisdomwalker. The principles are so profound that in the Divination Commission only the master diviner truly understands them.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So they're computers?
::'''March 7th:''' Seems like it, but "jade abacus" does sound a lot better.
::'''March 7th:''' Besides, ordinary computers don't have cool backstories. Technology handed down from Nous, huh...
::'''March 7th:''' Even in Madam Herta's space station, I never saw anything related to Nous.
::So they're just microchips?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So they're just microchips?
:'''Welt:''' It sounds like similar technology. Maybe we'll get a better understanding if we see the manufacturing process with our own eyes.
:'''Qingque:''' I'm afraid that's impossible &mdash; the Artisanship Commission's Hall of Jadeology keeps a close watch over the jade carving process.
:'''Qingque:''' But if you're interested, there's a shop selling jade abacus jewelry in Starskiff Haven &mdash; I can show you around when I'm free.
:'''March 7th:''' Did you hear that, (Trailblazer)? She said she's taking Mr. Yang jewelry shopping. Hehe, that'll be interesting.
:'''Qingque:''' Anyway, don't dwell on names. As long as the machine works, what does it matter whether it's a "jade abacus" or a "computer"?
:{{tx}}

;(Talk to Fu Xuan)
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Qingque, restarting the base terminals will be your responsibility.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Oh, and forget everything you saw and heard just now.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' I will guard the Matrix core. Once we've restarted the three terminals, Kafka's interrogation can commence.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' When we're finished, I'll give you enough time to talk to her.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What happens when you activate the Matrix of Prescience?
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' Once activated, the Matrix of Prescience analyzes all the information contained in the target &mdash; Kafka in this case &mdash; and transfers anything pertaining to the Xianzhou into the diviner's consciousness.
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' Every one of us walks a Path, moving ceaselessly through time and space, creating all manner of karma in our wake...
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' How are things progressing? I have yet to sense the connection between the three base terminals.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why not use it to calculate the location of the Stellaron?
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' Divination is no mere conjecture. If the parameters are insufficient and uncertainty surrounds the target, then it is like looking for a needle in a galaxy. Do you understand?
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' Furthermore, interference caused by the Stellaron spirits that infiltrated the Commission has greatly reduced the accuracy of our divination. The margin of error could be as high as 0.2%! I cannot tolerate such inaccuracies in our interpretations.
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' So, have you activated the terminals yet? Why is the Matrix of Prescience still unresponsive?
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} What if its calculations are incorrect?
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' There is no "what if"! ...Because nothing remains unforeseen.
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' The Matrix's algorithm is known as "the way of all change" &mdash; it accounts for every unpredictability on the Path of all things with uncountable enumerations. When your objects of measure are eras of time and oceans of stars, there are no true variables in the world.
:::'''Fu Xuan:''' ...No more questions! Have you activated the three terminals!?
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Выход}} Say no more. Seriously, please don't say anything else.
:<!--0.5-second delay-->
:'''Qingque:''' Wow, you're amazing Mr. Yang! You handled that well for an outsider. I officially hand over the title of "keeper of the loafing gate" to you!
{{Dialogue End}}

